e story of course as sully  is claiming to nurse old injuries turns  out getting old worked in mark's favor  and he plans to do so  gracefully number seven tom's stunts are  smashing in the barcelona chase scene  tom holland vaulted over a railing and  slid down a roof he ended up smashing  his hip into the tiles and his whole hip  was black and blue for a few weeks i  walked away from every stunt but i  definitely live from a few tom and  sophia could start a club number eight  we bet tom's got great calluses from all  these stunts now tom and everyone  involved ended up injuring themselves  from hanging onto the straps during the  airplane sequence all of us tore our  hands up tom also suffered from plenty  of bangs bruises and tears due to  crashing into things sophia agrees there  was hard physical stuff some falls some  hits it was tough number nine would you  take being hit in the knees for two  million dollars how about if it happened  17 times well tom was hit by a car you  guessed it 17 times to get one shot of  course the car wasn't real but the speed  of the machine or bonnet as tom called  it moving towards him was enough to  stress out his mom who was on set that  day saying do you not think they've got  it already can't they move on he called  the scene pretty impressive a lot of fun  and very painful but very rewarding  and it wasn't all that dangerous because  they did their due diligence to make  sure the car was safe and padded we  would take being hit in the knees for 17  million dollars after hearing that  number 10. tension on set was building  after wahlberg's gift was mistaken for  something  inappropriate the filming of uncharted  was incredibly demanding for tom holland  he was going to the gym in the morning  thinking oh my god i must have torn  something in my leg and the guys told  him that he hadn't he's just getting old  the physical tension led to an awkward  moment between him and wahlberg the  previous calvin klein underwear model  gave his co-star a massage gun but tom  had never seen one like it before and  mistook it as something else entirely  something a little more in the realm of  pleasure than tension number 11 turns  out spidey powers do come in handy  sometimes tom had to do far more than  stunt work for this movie than he had to  do for any other spider-man movies  because there's no mask or cgi to hide  behind his action sequences in uncharted  are the biggest he's ever been a part of  saying the cuts and bruises and bangs he  got from dangling off of wires and  falling off of things was ridiculous  number 12 the sticker tom got was  probably a band-aid tom didn't say how  it happened but he did bang his head  pretty bad on set but he was all right i  got a sticker saying bang my head at  work today what we want to know is who  was walking around on set giving out  these stickers  number 13 it isn't an action movie if  there isn't real danger on set of course  tom narrowly avoided worse injuries when  he found himself holding on for dear  life he struggled in that airplane  sequence because he was attached to  wires but was only just holding on to  the crates so the cougar arms that were  carrying the crates did different  motions like rock back and forth or spin  well they had different speed levels  since level four didn't feel all that  different from level five tom said that  wasn't that much harder do not do level  eight that's the moment tom realized  he'd made a terrible mistake he suddenly  found himself struggling to hold on  because the faster you spin the further  you fly and your odds of letting go and  flying into a crane are pretty good he  got off lucky though and no serious  injuries were reported  even still we think tom learned a  valuable lesson you don't go straight  from easy mode to extreme mode or you'll  drop from three lives down to zero very  quickly while mark wahlberg got to sit  back and nurse fake injuries the whole  movie poor tom was doing all of the 